course: dictionary
lesson: 15191
title: What is secularism?
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Secularism is the idea that religion should be kept separate from government, public schools and laws. A country that follows secularism does not run its laws or schools around one religion. «Our school teaches about many religions, but it does not belong to any one of them.» The clue is «teaches about many religions»: the school is fair to all faiths and favours none.
explain: Secularism can also be a way of living or thinking that is not based on religion. «Many people choose a secular view of the world, based on science and reason.» Secular is the adjective: a secular law, a secular school, a secular state. Read the words around it to see whether the text means the rules of a country or the beliefs of a person.
explain: Context helps again. «The country is a secular state, so people of any faith, or none, can live freely.» The words «any faith, or none» tell you a secular state does not force anyone to follow a religion. Always check your meaning by putting it in the sentence in place of the hard word.
fact: Secularism means keeping religion separate from government, public schools and laws.
fact: «Secular» describes something that is not connected with religion.
fact: A «secular state» lets people of any faith, or none, live freely.
fact: The USA and France keep church and state apart. The UK has an official church, the Church of England, but many of its laws are secular.
fact: Secularism does not mean being against religion; it means religion is kept separate from the state.
exercise: «The country is a secular state, so every citizen can choose their own faith.» What is a secular state? | A state where only one religion is allowed | *A state where people of any faith, or none, can live freely | A state with no laws at all | A state that is ruled by a church
exercise: «Our school teaches about many religions, but it does not belong to any one of them.» Which idea of secularism does this show? | The school is closed on holy days | *Religion is kept separate from the running of the school | The school only teaches prayer | The school must follow one religion's rules
exercise: Jordan says secularism means being against all religions. Is Jordan right? | Yes, it means hating religion | No, it means only the government has religion | Yes, it means everyone must pray | *No, it means keeping religion separate from government, schools and laws
test: «Her country is a secular state.» What does secular mean here? | Ruled by one king | Very old | Full of churches | *Not based on religion, with laws that do not favour one faith
test: Which word describes a way of thinking that is not based on religion? | sacred | curt | *secular | famished
exam: «The UK has an official church, but many of its laws are secular.» What does this sentence suggest? | Religion is banned everywhere | The UK has no laws at all | *Some laws are not based on religion, even though one church is official | All laws are based on the church
